task-124 activation batch id collision

ROOT CAUSE: activationBatchId was "activation-"+activationToken (per-attempt counter). Distinct
payloads reusing a counter value collided; host binds one payload per batch id (index.ts:24122).
HOST PATH: POST /api/role-model/endpoints/batch is correct for adding models to an existing provider
account; it appends endpoints for {providerAccountId, modelId} and returns committed. Unique ids fix it.

FIX: activationBatchId = activation-<token>-<FNV1a digest of activations> in both create and
key-updated paths.

TESTS s638 3/3: distinct ids for distinct payloads at the SAME token (RED captured with old ids),
exact bodies, fake host binding id->payload accepts both consecutive saves, saved state after activation.

FINAL: full UI suite 1010/1010; UI tsc 0. Packaged check (add a second DeepSeek model on the rebuild) still required by the build lane.
